EFG 2 R "Centipede game. Two inning, with probability of altruists.  " { "Player 1" "Player 2" }
"The 4-move centipede game from :cite:p:`McKPal92`, extended with the
incomplete-information altruism model of Section 4.1 (Appendix A, Figure 8):
each player is independently a rational payoff-maximizer with probability
19/20, or an altruist who always chooses PASS with probability 1/20. This
fixed parameterization is kept as an illustrative example, since Gambit's file
formats do not yet support symbolic payoffs or probabilities."

c "" 1 "(0,1)" { "1=rational" 19/20 "1=altruist" 1/20 } 0
c "" 2 "(0,2)" { "2=rational" 19/20 "2=altruist" 1/20 } 0
p "" 1 1 "(1,1)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 1 "Outcome 1" { 0.40, 0.10 }
p "" 2 1 "(2,1)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 2 "Outcome 2" { 0.20, 0.80 }
p "" 1 2 "(1,2)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 3 "Outcome 3" { 1.60, 0.40 }
p "" 2 2 "(2,2)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 4 "Outcome 4" { 0.80, 3.20 }
t "" 5 "Outcome 5" { 6.40, 1.60 }
p "" 1 1 "(1,1)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 6 "Outcome 11" { 0.40, 0.10 }
p "" 2 3 "(2,3)" { "p" } 0
p "" 1 2 "(1,2)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 7 "Outcome 13" { 1.60, 0.40 }
p "" 2 4 "(2,4)" { "p" } 0
t "" 5 "Outcome 5" { 6.40, 1.60 }
c "" 3 "(0,3)" { "2=rational" 19/20 "2=altruist" 1/20 } 0
p "" 1 3 "(1,3)" { "p" } 0
p "" 2 1 "(2,1)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 8 "Outcome 22" { 0.20, 0.80 }
p "" 1 4 "(1,4)" { "p" } 0
p "" 2 2 "(2,2)" { "t" "p" } 0
t "" 9 "Outcome 24" { 0.80, 3.20 }
t "" 5 "Outcome 5" { 6.40, 1.60 }
p "" 1 3 "(1,3)" { "p" } 0
p "" 2 3 "(2,3)" { "p" } 0
p "" 1 4 "(1,4)" { "p" } 0
p "" 2 4 "(2,4)" { "p" } 0
t "" 5 "Outcome 5" { 6.40, 1.60 }
